title Your team goes forward
intro Blue wins the ball and attacks.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player B-CM at 60, 34
  player R-CM at 68, 44
  ball with B-CM

step
  caption You are the defender in blue. Watch what happens.
  label B-CB You

step
  caption Blue's attack races off toward Red's goal, and you are left far behind.
  B-CM to 74, 34
  B-LF to 84, 24
  B-RF to 84, 46
  ball with B-CM
  arrow from B-CM to 90, 34
  arrow from B-LF to 96, 22
  arrow from B-RF to 96, 48
  duration 1200

step
  caption If you push up with them, the team stays close and Red has less space.
  B-CB to 50, 34
  arrow from 22, 34 to B-CB
  duration 1100

question
  prompt Why move up with the team?
  answer So everyone stays close together
  wrong So you can score the goal
  wrong Defenders must stay by the goalie
  wrong Red has to kick it out
  correct The team stays together.
  why Moving up keeps a small gap in front of you. Stay back and Red gets a huge empty field if they win the ball.

question
  prompt How far should you go?
  answer Up near the middle of the field
  wrong All the way into Red's box
  wrong Stay next to your goalie
  wrong Off the field
  correct Up near the middle.
  why If you keep running into their box, nobody is left at the back. Push up, but stay behind your midfielders.
